module akd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }
import frcrimp.deadlines.{ SentencingScheduled }

// The District of Alaska's own criminal periods, counted under the
// criminal rules (FRCrimP 45(a) governs "any local rule"). The local
// criminal rules supplement the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure, the
// Local Civil Rules and Local Magistrate Judge Rules apply where not
// inconsistent, and the court may change, dispense with or waive any of
// them in the interest of justice (L.Crim.R. 1.1(a), (b)). No trigger
// carries a service method: FRCrimP 45(c)'s three added days follow the
// manner of service, which is not modeled here.
//
// Periods that are FRCrimP periods stay in lit/frcrimp: FRCrimP 32(e)(2)'s
// 35-day presentence disclosure (psr-disclosure) is not restated; the
// local draft and final report periods below are the court's own.
//
// A period to a clock time stays in a note: the felony plea agreement,
// and any unsigned superseding charging document, is due by noon of the
// business day preceding the change-of-plea hearing (L.Crim.R. 11.2(a)(2),
// (c)); the counting rule declares no time of day for a day-counted
// period.
//
// Conditions that are not deadlines from an event stay in notes: a
// change of plea requires a Notice of Intent to Change Plea (L.Crim.R.
// 11.1(a)); sentencing is scheduled "approximately 90 days" after a guilty
// plea or verdict unless otherwise ordered (L.Crim.R. 32.1(a)), a target
// rather than a deadline; expert reports follow the Order of Progression
// (L.Crim.R. 16.1(a)); the court appoints CJA counsel when retained
// counsel has not appeared within 7 days of the initial appearance
// (L.Crim.R. 44.2(a)(1)), a condition of appointment rather than a party's
// deadline; no reply to an opposition is filed unless the court orders
// otherwise (L.Crim.R. 47.1(d)); chambers copies are required of every
// filing over 25 pages (L.Crim.R. 49.1(a)(3)). A motion to continue states
// the days remaining on the Speedy Trial Act clock (L.Crim.R. 47.1(a)),
// whose period stays in lit/frcrimp. The district's Speedy Trial Plan and
// CJA Plan are referred to (L.Crim.R. 44.2(b), 50.1(b)) but not vendored.
//
// The earlier D. Alaska criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// (United States v. Salerno, Brady v. Maryland, and the other FRCrimP,
// Speedy Trial Act and constitutional authority it named) belong to
// lit/frcrimp; they are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// A motion for reconsideration, and a response or reply the court
/// requests: at most 5 pages (D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)(2)-(4)).
limit reconsideration-paper {
  pages <= 5 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)"
} cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)"

/// The defendant's proposed change of plea from not guilty to guilty
/// (D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 11.1).
event ChangeOfPleaProposed()
/// The defendant is arraigned (D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 16.1(a)).
event Arraigned()
/// The date a blunt or edged weapon or similar exhibit is to be brought to
/// the courtroom (D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 23.1(b)).
event WeaponExhibitScheduled()
/// The date drugs, cash, firearms or a similar exhibit is to be brought to
/// the courtroom (D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 23.1(a)).
event SensitiveExhibitScheduled()
/// A petition alleging a violation of probation or supervised release is
/// filed while the person is in custody (D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1.1(a)).
event RevocationPetitionFiledInCustody()
/// A magistrate judge announces on the record a report and
/// recommendation after a referred revocation evidentiary hearing (D.
/// Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1.1(c)(2)).
event RevocationRecommendationAnnounced()
/// The disposition hearing on a revocation is scheduled (D. Alaska
/// L.Crim.R. 32.1.1(e)).
event DispositionHearingScheduled()
/// A motion to authorize release or disclosure of a presentence report is
/// filed (D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1.2(e)).
event PsrDisclosureMotionFiled()
/// A hearing at which a request for other pretrial release services, or a
/// proposed third-party custodian, is to be considered is scheduled (D.
/// Alaska L.Crim.R. 46.1(d), (e)).
event ReleaseServicesHearingScheduled()
/// The date of a defendant's or defense witness's intended non-custodial
/// travel (D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 46.2).
event IntendedTravel()
/// A pretrial motion is filed (D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(c)).
event PretrialMotionFiled()
/// A post-conviction motion, other than one under the habeas corpus local
/// rules, is filed (D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(c)).
event PostConvictionMotionFiled()
/// An order is entered (D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)(2)(A)).
event OrderEntered()
/// New material facts are discovered or the law changes (D. Alaska
/// L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)(2)(B)).
event NewFactsOrLawChange()
/// A motion for reconsideration is filed and served (D. Alaska L.Crim.R.
/// 47.1(g)(2)).
event ReconsiderationMotionFiled() paper reconsideration-paper
/// The court enters an order requesting a response to a motion for
/// reconsideration (D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)(3)).
event ReconsiderationResponseRequested()
/// The court orders a reply on a motion for reconsideration (D. Alaska
/// L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)(4)).
event ReconsiderationReplyRequested()
/// A motion to submit a document for in camera review is granted (D.
/// Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(j)(3)).
event InCameraReviewGranted()
/// A magistrate judge issues a report and recommendation (D. Alaska
/// L.Crim.R. 59.1).
event RecommendationIssued()
/// Objections to a magistrate judge's report and recommendation are filed
/// (D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 59.1).
event RecommendationObjectionsFiled()

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 11.1(b): defense counsel arranges a presentence
/// investigation interview to occur within 14 days following the proposed
/// change of plea.
deadline presentence-interview: 14.days after ChangeOfPleaProposed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 11.1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 16.1(a): the discovery materials FRCrimP 16 lists,
/// exclusive of expert reports, are provided to the defense within 14
/// calendar days after the arraignment.
deadline rule16-discovery: 14.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 16.1(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 23.1(a): a party wishing to introduce drugs, cash,
/// firearms or similar items contacts the U.S. Marshal for instructions not
/// later than 2 business days before the date the item is to be brought to
/// the courtroom.
deadline sensitive-exhibit-marshal-contact: 2.business_days before SensitiveExhibitScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 23.1(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 23.1(b): a party wishing to introduce blunt or
/// edged weapons or similar items contacts the U.S. Marshal not later than
/// 1 week before the date the item is to be brought to the courtroom.
deadline weapon-exhibit-marshal-contact: 7.days before WeaponExhibitScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 23.1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1(b): the draft presentence report is disclosed
/// to counsel not less than 42 days before the sentencing date.
deadline draft-psr-disclosure: 42.days before SentencingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1(c): the final presentence report is disclosed
/// to counsel not less than 21 days before the sentencing date; the
/// confidential sentencing recommendation is disclosed with it unless
/// otherwise ordered (L.Crim.R. 32.1(d)).
deadline final-psr-disclosure: 21.days before SentencingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1(e)(1): not less than 7 days before the
/// sentencing hearing, each party files and serves a sentencing
/// memorandum, with its sealed addendum (L.Crim.R. 32.1(f)); a motion for
/// an evidentiary hearing is due with it (L.Crim.R. 32.1(h)).
deadline sentencing-memorandum: 7.days before SentencingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1(e)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1(e)(2): not less than 3 days before the
/// sentencing hearing, each party may reply to the opposing sentencing
/// memorandum.
deadline sentencing-reply: 3.days before SentencingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1(e)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1.1(a)(2)(A): if the person is in custody, the
/// initial appearance on a revocation petition is held without
/// unnecessary delay, and in no case more than 7 days after the petition
/// is filed, absent extenuating circumstances.
deadline revocation-initial-appearance: 7.days after RevocationPetitionFiledInCustody() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1.1(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1.1(c)(2)(A): an objection to a magistrate
/// judge's report and recommendation on a revocation violation is filed
/// within 7 days of the date announced; without a timely objection the
/// court may adopt it without further hearing (L.Crim.R. 32.1.1(c)(2)(B)).
deadline revocation-recommendation-objection: 7.days after RevocationRecommendationAnnounced() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1.1(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1.1(e)(2)(A): unless otherwise ordered, the
/// Sentencing Recommendation for Violation Disposition is filed not less
/// than 7 days before the disposition hearing.
deadline violation-recommendation-filing: 7.days before DispositionHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1.1(e)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1.1(e)(2)(B): unless otherwise ordered, a party
/// with significant legal or factual disputes with the Sentencing
/// Recommendation files a disposition memorandum not less than 2 business
/// days before the disposition hearing.
deadline disposition-memorandum: 2.business_days before DispositionHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1.1(e)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1.2(e)(2)(D): any interested party may file and
/// serve an opposition to the release or disclosure of a presentence
/// report within 14 days of the date the motion is filed.
deadline psr-disclosure-opposition: 14.days after PsrDisclosureMotionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 32.1.2(e)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 46.1(d)(1): counsel requesting other release
/// services gives Pretrial Services and opposing counsel a written request
/// no less than 4 business days before the hearing at which it is
/// considered; the third-party custodian forms are served on the same
/// timetable (L.Crim.R. 46.1(e)(3)).
deadline release-services-request: 4.business_days before ReleaseServicesHearingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 46.1(d)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 46.2: a request for non-custodial travel of a
/// federal defendant or a defense witness is filed at least 10 days in
/// advance of the intended travel, except on a showing of good cause.
deadline travel-request: 10.days before IntendedTravel() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 46.2"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(c): unless otherwise ordered, an opposition to
/// a pretrial motion is filed within 7 days of the filing of the motion.
deadline pretrial-opposition: 7.days after PretrialMotionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(c): unless otherwise ordered, an opposition to
/// a post-conviction motion (other than one under the habeas corpus local
/// rules) is filed within 14 days of the filing of the motion.
deadline post-conviction-opposition: 14.days after PostConvictionMotionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)(2)(A): a motion for reconsideration for
/// manifest error of law or fact is filed and served not later than 7
/// days after the entry of the order.
deadline reconsideration-manifest-error: 7.days after OrderEntered() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)(2)(B): a motion for reconsideration on new
/// material facts or an intervening change in the law is filed and served
/// within 14 days of the discovery or change in law.
deadline reconsideration-new-facts: 14.days after NewFactsOrLawChange() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)(3): no response to a motion for
/// reconsideration is filed unless the court requests one; unless
/// otherwise ordered, it is filed within 7 days of entry of the order
/// requesting it.
deadline reconsideration-response: 7.days after ReconsiderationResponseRequested() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)(4): no reply is filed unless the court
/// requests one; unless otherwise ordered, it is filed within 7 days of
/// the order requesting it.
deadline reconsideration-reply: 7.days after ReconsiderationReplyRequested() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(g)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(j)(3): if a motion to submit documents in
/// camera is granted, the documents are filed through CM/ECF as an ex
/// parte document within 7 days.
deadline in-camera-filing: 7.days after InCameraReviewGranted() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 47.1(j)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 59.1: unless otherwise ordered, a party may file
/// objections within 14 days after the issuance of a magistrate judge's
/// report and recommendation; the district court then determines the
/// matter under FRCrimP 59(b).
deadline recommendation-objection: 14.days after RecommendationIssued() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 59.1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 59.1: the opposing party may respond to the
/// objections within 7 days of their filing.
deadline recommendation-objection-response: 7.days after RecommendationObjectionsFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Alaska L.Crim.R. 59.1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
